Library statusprobe version "0.1".

(A shared library that reads `the reaped status` and nothing else. It
 exists to test LANGUAGE.md's claim that the -1 sentinel lives in
 loader-initialized .data rather than .bss: `_start` — which would zero a
 .bss global — is only emitted for executables, so a library reading a
 .bss sentinel would see 0 and report "exited cleanly" with no child ever
 reaped. Built with:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/fixtures/statusprobe.vox --shared \
   -o docs/ledger/probes/process-control/fixtures/libstatusprobe.so)

To 'the status a library sees'.
  Return a number, the reaped status.
